Error [E0129]: `StrongId` can't be built on `UserId` — `UserId` is itself a distinct type
  --> tests/ui/distinct_over_distinct.jet:2:22
    |
  2 | StrongId #= distinct UserId;
    |                      ^^^^^^
 Why: `distinct`-over-`distinct` chaining is not allowed in v1; `UserId` is already a distinct type
 Fix: use `UserId` directly, or build on the shared base type

Error [E0119]: there's no type called `StrongId`
  --> tests/ui/distinct_over_distinct.jet:5:4
    |
  5 | x: StrongId #= StrongId(UserId(1))
    |    ^^^^^^^^
 Why: the types are `Int`, `Float`, `Bool`, and `String` (plus types you define)
 Fix: check the spelling, or define the struct or enum first

Error [E0102]: nothing named `StrongId` exists here
  --> tests/ui/distinct_over_distinct.jet:5:16
    |
  5 | x: StrongId #= StrongId(UserId(1))
    |                ^^^^^^^^
 Why: only functions that have been defined (or built in, like `print` / `input`) can be called
 Fix: define it first (fn StrongId() { ... }), or call one that exists
